# Frontend environment variables (Vite).
#
# Copy to .env for local overrides. Everything here is OPTIONAL for local
# development — with no .env at all the app falls back to the local backend,
# so `npm run dev` works out of the box.
#
# IMPORTANT: Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to client code,
# and it inlines them at BUILD time. These end up in the shipped bundle and
# are readable by anyone — never put a secret here.

# Backend ORIGIN (no trailing slash, no /api/v1 suffix — that's appended in
# src/lib/constants.js). Leave unset locally; set it in the deploy provider's
# build environment (e.g. Vercel project settings) to point at the real
# backend. Because it's inlined at build time, changing it requires a rebuild,
# not just a restart.
#
# Local default when unset: http://localhost:8000
# Production example:       https://your-backend.onrender.com
VITE_API_URL=
